  "limitations": [
    "Single configured endpoint/controller, RF1 logical partition leader/replica/ISR, epoch0 and no offline replicas; no wire Produce/Fetch, placement or replication claim.",
    "CreateTopics is partial against Apache2-7: supports2-4; nonempty configuration overrides return INVALID_CONFIG rather than fabricated config success.",
    "Automatic topic creation disabled; no authorizer/ACL enforcement; authorization bitmaps describe this no-authorizer local policy.",
    "Custom process-local catalog journal and trusted operator path; no distributed ownership, cross-process lock or Apache metadata-log format. Topic names never become paths.",
    "Each topic operation is atomic after sync; a multi-topic request is not a transaction. Timeout/cancellation after admitted commit can lose a receipt and is ambiguous until lookup/restart.",
    "Shutdown requires explicit stop/drain/join for deterministic completion; Drop requests stop and does not blockingly join. Actor queue, aggregate request bytes, responses and catalog history budgets bound local work.",
    "Actor tests model queue/cancellation/receipt/join faults. Catalog physical sync ambiguity belongs to KL11-59/KL11-03; orderly live restarts do not inject power loss.",
    "Official Apache serializers/parsers and selected request/name components execute independently. Ordinary single-node golden responses are policy assembled, not executed upstream controller responses; ordering is locally deterministic.",
    "Metadata12/13 null-name/zero-ID selectors are schema accepted by Apache components but locally fail closed before response encoding. Historical malformed response frames are excluded from positive qualification.",
    "Pinned librdkafka2.15 flexible all-topics Metadata uses a four-byte null-array reservation. Exactly three zero tail bytes are admitted for flexible null/all selectors after complete parsing; every other suffix/named/empty/classic selector and all mutating admin requests remain strict.",
    "RFC4122v4 IDs use approved broker-only getrandom0.4.3, at most32 attempts including collisions, and reservedzero/one/leading-base64url-minus exclusions; OS entropy and filesystem sync guarantees are inherited.",
    "No security, cluster durability, full Apache controller behavior, production readiness or performance qualification. The checked registry explicitly retains qualification not_run."
  ]
